ramb bundles the following third-party code, taken in unchanged (fishycode
plan 013, "One distance function", 2026-10-09: a deliberate exception to the
recode rule — recoding Karney's numerics by hand is where errors would enter):

src/geodesic.c
src/geodesic.h
  GeographicLib-C, version 2.2
  https://github.com/geographiclib/geographiclib-c/tree/v2.2
  Copyright (c) Charles Karney (2012-2025) <karney@alum.mit.edu>
  License: MIT/X11 — the licence text is in the files' headers.

ramb recodes (does not copy) this third-party code:

src/trip_cnr.cpp (rb_cut_trip_voyages(method = "cnr"))
  The trip rule of create_fishing_trip() and its helpers in
  R-dev/galdelli_pulcinella_tassetti/R/global_functions.R of the ICES Workshop
  WKSSFGEO, branch dev_branch (R4AIS v1.0.1, doi 10.5281/zenodo.4757505),
  by A. Galdelli, J. Pulcinella, A.N. Tassetti and E. Armelloni (CNR-IRBIM).
  License: GNU GPL 3, the folder's own licence, as ramb's GPL (>= 3) allows.

R/trip.R (rb_cut_trip_voyages(method = "iapesca"))
  The trip rule of Detect_FishingTrips(), CleanSpuriousSpeeds() and CalcSpeed()
  of the R package iapesca 0.1 by Julien Rodriguez (Ifremer),
  https://github.com/JulRodrigu/r-packages_iapesca, commit 1b7248c, recoded as
  DuckDB SQL. License: GPL (its DESCRIPTION), as ramb's GPL (>= 3) allows.

ramb also ships these third-party datasets in inst/extdata, as parquet, read
with rb_read_example(); data-raw/labelled_tracks.R and data-raw/extdata.R make
them from the sources. Their full citations, as BibTeX, are in REFERENCES.bib;
each dataset's help page and data dictionary entry (inst/extdata/data-dict.yaml)
name them:

inst/extdata/dansk.parquet
inst/extdata/dansk_harbours.parquet
  From example_data_AIS.csv and the harbours of the ICES Workshop WKSSFGEO,
  https://github.com/ices-eg/WKSSFGEO.
  Copyright (c) 2021 ICES Expert Groups. License: MIT (text below).

inst/extdata/creel.parquet
  From Mendo T., Smout S., Photopoulou T., James M. (2019). Data from:
  Identifying fishing grounds from vessel tracks: model-based inference for
  small scale fisheries. Dryad, https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.k80bp46.
  License: CC0 1.0.

inst/extdata/wkssfgeo2_it_pots.parquet
  From IT_CNR_2023_GP.csv (CNR-IRBIM) of the ICES Workshop WKSSFGEO2,
  https://github.com/ices-eg/WKSSFGEO2, commit f3e49fe.
  Copyright (c) 2023 ICES Expert Groups. License: MIT (text below).

inst/extdata/wkssfgeo_pt_gps.parquet
  From example_data_GPS.csv of the ICES Workshop WKSSFGEO,
  https://github.com/ices-eg/WKSSFGEO, commit 3da870d.
  Copyright (c) 2021 ICES Expert Groups. License: MIT (text below).

inst/extdata/wkssfgeo_adriatic_passive.parquet
inst/extdata/wkssfgeo_denmark.parquet
  From data-examples/passive_vessel_ais_adriatic_2017.csv and data/Denmark.rds
  of the ICES Workshop WKSSFGEO, https://github.com/ices-eg/WKSSFGEO, commit
  3da870d. Copyright (c) 2021 ICES Expert Groups. License: MIT (text below).

inst/extdata/wkssfgeo2_irl_pots.parquet
inst/extdata/wkssfgeo2_irl_gillnets.parquet
inst/extdata/wkssfgeo2_pt_gps.parquet
  From IRL_FPO_WKSSFGEO2_Anon.csv, IRL_KY22_WKSSFGEO2_Anon.csv and
  PT_IPM_2017_GP2.csv of the ICES Workshop WKSSFGEO2,
